Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:38:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] downloads: Animeko-style progress notification with speed and
 progress
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Unify the download notification with the HarmonyOS builds of Animeko
and Mihon so that the three apps read alike in the notification shade:

- title: "Downloading N episodes" (queued + active)
- text: "Download: <speed>/s · <progress>%" with a determinate progress
  bar; while ffmpeg has not reported a percentage yet (or the duration is
  unknown) the text shows the speed alone over an indeterminate bar
- expanded text additionally shows the current "<anime> - <episode>"
  (omitted when "hide notification content" is enabled)

Speed comes from DownloadSpeedMeter (3 s sliding window, same file as
Mihon) fed with the byte deltas of ffmpeg's StatisticsCallback. The
per-download 50 ms ticker is replaced by a single 1 Hz ticker in the
downloader job, and the notifier drops updates for the same episode
that arrive within 700 ms.
